From 319be0254324806ee877b4f13031ec8c45cf03df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VCKing101 <59761021+VCKing101@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 15:48:22 +1030
Subject: [PATCH] Renderer: a Vulkan report when it cannot start, and a hook to
 say so

When the renderer could not start, the game ran on with no window. A
player saw nothing happen: the program stayed in Task Manager, waiting
unseen at the game's first dialog, and the log said only what SDL said.
Issue 24 of the Dissidia 012 port was this: a GTX 1070 on a current
driver, and "Installed Vulkan doesn't implement the VK_KHR_surface
extension", which means the loader found no driver at all.

The log now gets a report of what the machine has for Vulkan
(gpu/vulkan_report.cpp, "[vulkan]" lines): the graphics adapters as DXGI
lists them, with their drivers' versions; the loader's version and
instance extensions; the loader's own account of its driver search,
which manifests it found and which drivers it loaded or skipped and why;
the devices of an instance made without a window; and those of the
loader's environment variables that are set. VK_LOADER_DEBUG is read
once, when the loader is loaded at start-up, so the account comes from a
debug messenger chained into vkCreateInstance, which the loader gives
the same messages; only its problems and its driver lines are kept.

GameProfile::renderer_unavailable is called with the renderer's reason
when the game starts without a renderer (not when <prefix>_NO_RENDER
turns it off), after the report. A player's build can tell the player
and end. Without the hook nothing changes: the game runs on without a
window, as test runs on a machine without Vulkan want. The setup screens
still fall back to the system's dialogs when they find no renderer; only
the game's own start calls the hook.

Tested on Windows 11 with Dissidia 012 (setup build, llvm-mingw), AMD
and Intel graphics: VK_DRIVER_FILES pointing at no file gives the
reporter's exact error, the report names the variable and "Found no
drivers!", and the port's hook shows its message and ends; a normal
start is unchanged. hle_media.cpp also compiles without the renderer.
Not tested: Linux, macOS, a real broken driver install, another game.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
